(Query Optimisation and Indexing) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Query optimisation is central to advanced database systems. The query planner estimates) Tj T*
(the cost of several plans and picks the cheapest one for each query.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An index is a separate data structure, often a b-tree, that speeds up retrieval at the) Tj T*
(cost of extra storage and slower writes. A partial index covers only the rows that match) Tj T*
(a condition.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Use EXPLAIN ANALYZE to display the query plan and the real run time. Concurrency control) Tj T*
(and transaction processing decide how many queries can safely run at the same time in a) Tj T*
(distributed database.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
